## Rules in force

1. Write `MEMORY.md` and `DECISIONS.md` only through `.agents/skills/project-memory/scripts/memory.py`; never edit, renumber or delete an entry by hand. (origin: [D001](DECISIONS.md#d001--adopt-the-ems-project-memory-system))
2. When something needs clarifying, ask instead of assuming; one question, then wait. (origin: [D001](DECISIONS.md#d001--adopt-the-ems-project-memory-system))
3. Say so when the user's idea has a problem or a better option exists, with the reason; do not agree by default. (origin: [D001](DECISIONS.md#d001--adopt-the-ems-project-memory-system))
4. Before a change that touches several files or whose approach is not obvious, get a plan from `project-planner`, show it to the user exactly as it came (same format, checkboxes and labels; do not summarise or reformat it) and wait for their OK; then `project-plan-executor` carries it out, saving it in `plans/` with the evidence of every step. (origin: [D001](DECISIONS.md#d001--adopt-the-ems-project-memory-system))
5. Change, add or remove a rule of this file only together with the decision in `DECISIONS.md` that changes it, following record step 5 of `.agents/skills/project-memory/SKILL.md`; every rule ends with `(origin: <link>)`. (origin: [D001](DECISIONS.md#d001--adopt-the-ems-project-memory-system))
